    "# Adaptive line reconstruction from synthetic 128×128 raster images\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook generates synthetic images containing up to **5 random straight vectors**. Each vector is rasterised as a **1-pixel black line on a white background**.\n",
    "\n",
    "This version includes:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `IMG_SIZE = 128`\n",
    "- no fixed random seed, so the synthetic data changes every full run\n",
    "- a minimum reconstructed vector rule, so paths with only 1 or 2 pixels are ignored\n",
    "- large visual-debug panels for visual inspection\n",
    "\n",
    "The reconstruction pipeline is intentionally interpretable:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Threshold raster pixels into dots.\n",
    "2. Build an 8-neighbour pixel graph.\n",
    "3. Detect endpoints and intersections.\n",
    "4. Trace paths between nodes.\n",
    "5. Fit average vectors through traced pixel paths.\n",
    "6. Reject very short paths/vectors.\n",
    "7. Rasterise the predicted vectors again for comparison.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "820e0654",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import random\n",
    "import math\n",
    "from collections import deque, defaultdict\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "# No fixed seed = new synthetic data every time the notebook kernel is restarted and run from the top.\n",
    "# Set SEED to an integer, e.g. 42, only when you want repeatable results.\n",
    "SEED = None\n",
    "if SEED is not None:\n",
    "    random.seed(SEED)\n",
    "    np.random.seed(SEED)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Image/data settings\n",
    "IMG_SIZE = 128\n",
    "MAX_LINES = 5\n",
    "LINE_WEIGHT = 1\n",
    "N_TRAIN = 500\n",
    "N_TEST = 100\n",
    "\n",
    "# Minimum predicted line rule.\n",
    "# This prevents a predicted vector from being created from only 1 or 2 adjacent pixels.\n",
    "MIN_LINE_PIXELS = 3\n",
    "MIN_LINE_LENGTH = 2.0  # 3 adjacent pixel positions span 2 pixels of Euclidean distance.\n",
    "\n",
    "# Display settings\n",
    "DEBUG_DPI = 130\n",
    "DEBUG_FIGSIZE = (24, 5.5)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Using IMG_SIZE = {IMG_SIZE}x{IMG_SIZE}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Minimum predicted path pixels = {MIN_LINE_PIXELS}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Minimum predicted vector span = {MIN_LINE_LENGTH} pixels\")\n"
   ]
